.\" EazyMake manual page -- ezmk(1)
.\" Written for EazyMake 1.4.3.
.\" Keep in sync with src/cli.cpp: run scripts/check_man_sync.py before
.\" committing changes to this file or to the CLI option specs.
.TH EZMK 1 "2026-09-19" "EazyMake 1.4.3" "User Commands"
.\" Disable hyphenation: this page is full of copy-pasteable option names.
.nh
.SH NAME
ezmk \- a simple C/C++ build tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezmk
.I command
[
.I subcommand
] [
.I options
] [
.I arguments
]
.br
.B ezmk
.I shorthand
[
.I options
] [
.I arguments
]
.br
.B ezmk
.I action
[
.I options
] [
.I arguments
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezmk
builds C and C++ projects from a single declarative
.B ezmk.toml
file: it collects sources, compiles them in parallel, links the final
artifact and keeps an incremental cache under
.BR .ezmk/ .
There is no build script to write and no build directory to create.
.PP
The compiler is detected automatically
.RB ( gcc ,
.BR clang " or " cl.exe )
and the same
.B ezmk.toml
works across toolchains; MSVC differences are handled by a flag
translation layer plus an optional
.B msvc_flags
escape hatch.
.PP
.B Project root discovery.
Commands that operate on a project look for
.B ezmk.toml
in the current directory and then walk up at most
.B 5
parent directories, so
.B ezmk build
works from a source subdirectory. A directory containing only
.B ezmk\-workspace.toml
is a workspace container: use
.B ezmk workspace
or the
.B \-w
redirect in that case.
.PP
.B Language.
Diagnostics and help text follow the system locale and can be forced with
.BR EZMK_LANG .
The full command reference is documented in
.IR docs/en/cli.md ,
and the configuration file in
.BR ezmk.toml (5).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Daily builds
.TP
.B ezmk build [options]
Incremental build (compile and link). Full form:
.BR "ezmk project build" .
.TP
.B ezmk run [options] [\-\- args]
Build and run the program. Full form:
.BR "ezmk project run" .
.TP
.B ezmk clean
Discard the incremental cache: removes
.B .ezmk/cache
and the temporary build directory. Full form:
.BR "ezmk project clean" ;
.B \-w
redirects to
.BR "ezmk workspace clean" .
.TP
.B ezmk watch [options]
Rebuild automatically when a source file, header, or
.B ezmk.toml
changes (300 ms debounce). Full form:
.BR "ezmk project watch" .
.TP
.B ezmk install [options]
Install build artifacts (binary, libraries, headers) below the configured
prefix. Full form:
.BR "ezmk project install" .
.TP
.B ezmk test [options]
Build and run the project test suite. Full form:
.BR "ezmk project test" .
.TP
.B ezmk pack [options]
Create a distributable archive. Full form:
.BR "ezmk project pack" .
.SS Project
.TP
.BI "ezmk project new [options] " name
Scaffold a new project directory.
.TP
.B ezmk project cc [options]
Generate
.B compile_commands.json
for clangd and other language servers.
.TP
.BI "ezmk project export [options] " "<cmake|vscode>"
Generate build configuration from
.BR ezmk.toml :
a
.B CMakeLists.txt
or the
.B .vscode/
debug trio (launch, tasks, settings).
.TP
.B ezmk project import [options]
Import an existing CMake project into
.BR ezmk.toml .
Experimental: constructs that cannot be mapped abort the import without
writing anything.
.SS Packages
.TP
.BI "ezmk pkg install [options] " "file|url|name"
Install a package from a local archive or directory, a download URL, a
registered repository (by name) or a git repository URL.
.TP
.BI "ezmk pkg remove [options] " name
Remove an installed package.
.TP
.BI "ezmk pkg search [options] " name
Search the registered repositories.
.TP
.BI "ezmk pkg info [options] " name
Show details for a package.
.TP
.B ezmk pkg list [options]
List installed packages.
.TP
.BI "ezmk pkg update [options] " name
Update one package, or every installed package with
.BR \-\-all .
.SS Repositories
.TP
.BI "ezmk repo add [options] " url_or_path
Register a package repository (git URL or local directory).
.TP
.BI "ezmk repo remove [options] " name
Unregister a repository.
.TP
.BI "ezmk repo update [options] " name
Refresh repository indices; without a name, all of them.
.TP
.B ezmk repo list [options]
List registered repositories.
.TP
.BI "ezmk repo info [options] " name
Show repository details.
.SS Workspaces
.TP
.B ezmk workspace list
List the members declared in
.BR ezmk\-workspace.toml .
.TP
.B ezmk workspace build [options]
Build all members in topological order, in parallel.
.TP
.B ezmk workspace test [options]
Run the tests of every member.
.TP
.B ezmk workspace watch [options]
Watch every member and rebuild on change.
.TP
.B ezmk workspace clean [options]
Clean every member in reverse dependency order.
.TP
.BI "ezmk workspace scan [options] " dir
[options] [ dir ]
Adopt an existing directory tree: create or update
.BR ezmk\-workspace.toml .
.SS Other
.TP
.BI "ezmk utils " name " [args...]"
Run a Lua\-based tool provided by an installed
.B type = utils
package. Everything after the tool name is passed through to the tool;
.B \-\-
ends option parsing.
.TP
.BI "ezmk example [options] " name
[ name ] [options]
Scaffold one of the built\-in examples, or list them with
.BR list .
.TP
.B ezmk help
Print the usage summary (also
.BR \-h " / " \-\-help ).
.TP
.B ezmk version
Print the version (also
.BR \-V " / " \-\-version ).
.SH OPTIONS
Booleans take no value; options that take a value accept both
.B \-\-flag=value
and
.BR "\-\-flag value" .
.SS Global options
.TP
.BR \-\-color= \fImode\fR
Colorize output. Values:
.BR always " (alias " enable ),
.BR auto " (alias " default ,
the default) and
.BR never " (alias " disable ).
Case\-insensitive. An explicit
.B always
or
.B never
overrides the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable; only
.B auto
honors it.
.SS Common build options
Accepted by
.BR build ,
.B run
and
.BR watch .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the full compile and link commands, cache hits and misses, and, for
.BR build ,
a per\-file timing breakdown of the units that were actually compiled.
.TP
.BR \-j " \fIN\fR, " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Maximum number of parallel compile jobs.
.B 0
means automatic (hardware concurrency), which is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-cache
Recompile every source file. No cache entries are written and
.B record.json
is left empty, so the next ordinary build compiles everything again.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " \fIname\fR"
Apply a build profile declared in
.B [compile.profile.\fIname\fR]
and
.BR [link.profile.\fIname\fR] .
The profile must exist under
.BR [compile.profile.*] ;
a link\-only profile is rejected.
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-update
Run
.B ezmk repo update \-pug
before building.
.TP
.B \-\-compile\-commands
Write
.B compile_commands.json
after a successful build, for this invocation only (one\-shot equivalent of
.BR "[compile] compile_commands = true" ).
.SS ezmk project build
In addition to the common build options:
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workspace
Redirect to
.BR "ezmk workspace build" ;
equivalent to
.BR "ezmk build \-w" .
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-on\-error
Workspace redirect only: stop dispatching after the first failing member.
.TP
.BR \-\-member " \fIname\fR"
Workspace redirect only: build the named member and its dependency closure.
.SS ezmk project run
Accepts the common build options only. Everything after
.B \-\-
is passed to the program.
.SS ezmk project watch
In addition to the common build options:
.TP
.B \-\-no\-build\-on\-start
Skip the initial build and only watch for changes.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run
Run the freshly built executable after every successful rebuild (blocking;
watching resumes when it exits). Valid only for
.B type = executable
projects, and the initial build does not run. Arguments after
.B \-\-
are passed to the program on every run.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workspace
Redirect to
.BR "ezmk workspace watch" .
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-on\-error
Workspace redirect only, as for
.BR "ezmk build" .
.TP
.BR \-\-member " \fIname\fR"
Workspace redirect only, as for
.BR "ezmk build" .
.SS ezmk project test
.TP
.BR \-f " \fIframework\fR, " \-\-framework " \fIframework\fR"
Override
.B [test].framework
for this run:
.B catch2
or
.BR ezmk .
.TP
.BR \-\-filter " \fIpattern\fR"
Run only matching tests. For
.B catch2
this is a test\-name filter; for the built\-in
.B ezmk
framework it is a plain filename substring (no wildcards).
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " \fIname\fR"
Override
.B [test].default_profile
for this run.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-V ", " \-\-verbose
Print the compile and link commands of the test build and the standard
output of each test. The Catch2 runner is deliberately
.B not
given
.BR \-s ,
so passing cases are not listed individually. Note that
.B \-V
means \fIverbose\fR here, while at the top level
.B \-V
means \fIversion\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-report " \fIfmt\fR[:\fIpath\fR]"
Write a machine\-readable test report. The
.B ezmk
framework supports
.BR junit ;
the
.B catch2
framework also accepts any Catch2 reporter name
.RB ( json ", " xml ", " sonarqube ", ...)."
A relative
.I path
resolves against the project root. The report never changes the exit
status.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workspace
Redirect to
.BR "ezmk workspace test" .
.TP
.BR \-j " \fIN\fR, " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR, " \-\-stop\-on\-error ", " \-\-member " \fIname\fR"
Workspace redirect only, as for
.BR "ezmk workspace build" .
.SS ezmk project new
.TP
.BR \-\-type " \fItype\fR"
Project type:
.BR executable " (default), " static ", " shared " or " utils .
Each type scaffolds a different source layout.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-git\-init
Do not run
.B git init
in the new project.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-gitignore
Do not generate a
.BR .gitignore .
.SS ezmk project install
.TP
.BR \-\-prefix " \fIpath\fR"
Override
.BR [install].prefix .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be installed without copying anything.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-headers
Do not install headers.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-data
Accepted but currently a no\-op: data\-file installation is not implemented.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the files being installed.
.SS ezmk project pack
.TP
.BR \-\-output " \fIdir\fR"
Output directory (default
.BR . ).
.TP
.B \-\-precompiled
Produce a prebuilt archive
.RB ( include/
and
.BR lib/ )
instead of the default platform\-independent source package. Only valid for
.BR "type = static" .
.TP
.BR \-\-format " \fItar.gz|tgz|zip\fR"
Archive format; the default is
.BR tar.gz ,
and
.B tgz
is a case\-insensitive alias for it. Every format writes a
.B <archive>.sha256
sidecar.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the staged files and the archive command.
.SS ezmk project cc
.TP
.BR \-o " \fIpath\fR, " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Output file (default
.BR compile_commands.json
in the project root).
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " \fIname\fR"
Apply a build profile when computing the compile flags.
.SS ezmk project export
.TP
.BR \-o " \fIpath\fR, " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Output path (cmake target only).
.TP
.B \-\-profile " \fIname\fR"
Apply a build profile when generating the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing generated files.
.TP
.BR \-\-resolve ", " \-\-glob ", " \-\-no\-glob
cmake target only: resolve
.B @link:
paths to absolute paths, collect sources with a recursive glob, or emit an
explicit source list instead.
.SS ezmk project import
.TP
.BR \-\-from " \fIformat\fR"
Source format; currently only
.B cmake
(case\-insensitive).
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Overwrite an existing
.BR ezmk.toml .
.SS ezmk example
.TP
.BR \-o " \fIdir\fR, " \-\-output " \fIdir\fR"
Directory to scaffold into (default
.BR . ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage of this command and list the available examples.
.SS Package and repository options
.TP
.B scope flags
.BR \-p ", " \-u " and " \-g
select the project, user or global scope (see
.BR "SCOPE FLAGS" ).
.B pkg install
and
.B repo add
accept exactly one and default to the project scope; the other scoped
commands accept combinations such as
.B \-pug
and default to all three scopes.
.TP
.BR \-\-sha256 " \fIhash\fR"
.B pkg install
only: verify the archive against this SHA\-256 hash before installing.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
.BR pkg " " install
and
.BR "pkg update" :
skip all confirmation prompts. Accepted by
.B pkg update
since 1.4.2.
.TP
.B \-\-locked
.B pkg install
only: install only what the existing
.B ezmk.lock
pins, and fail on any mismatch.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lock
.B pkg install
only: do not create or update
.BR ezmk.lock .
.TP
.BR \-\-branch " \fIref\fR"
.B pkg install
only: for git URLs, clone this branch, tag or commit; it wins over a
.B #ref
fragment in the URL.
.TP
.B \-\-all
.B pkg update
only: update every installed package. Without a package name and without
.BR \-\-all ,
.B pkg update
fails. The command exits non\-zero when any update failed.
.TP
.BR \-\-name " \fIname\fR"
.B repo add
only: register the repository under this name instead of the name derived
from the URL.
.TP
.BR \-\-branch " \fIref\fR"
.B repo add
only: check out this branch, tag or commit of a git repository.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print detailed progress for every package and repository command.
.SS Workspace options
.TP
.BR \-j " \fIN\fR, " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Intra\-layer parallelism. Precedence:
.BR \-j " > " "[workspace.options].default_jobs" " > hardware concurrency."
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-on\-error
Stop dispatching new member tasks after the first failure; running members
finish naturally. Supported by
.B workspace build
and
.BR "workspace test" ,
not by
.BR "workspace clean" .
.TP
.BR \-\-member " \fIname\fR"
Select one member plus its dependency closure. Repeatable; both the full
relative path and the member basename are accepted.
.TP
.BR \-\-report " \fIfmt\fR[:\fIpath\fR]"
.B workspace test
only: forward a test report to every member.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run
.B workspace watch
only: forward
.B \-\-run
to executable members.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
.B workspace scan
only: print what would be written without touching the file.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
.B workspace scan
only: skip the confirmation prompt before merging into an existing
.BR ezmk\-workspace.toml .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print detailed workspace progress. Watchers are started one thread per
selected member, so
.B \-j
does not cap
.B workspace watch
concurrency.
.SH SCOPE FLAGS
Packages and repositories are installed per scope:
.TP
.B \-p
Project scope:
.BR <project>/.ezmk/pkg/
and
.BR <project>/.ezmk/repo/ .
.TP
.B \-u
User scope:
.B \(ti/.local/ezmk/pkg/
on Unix,
.B %LOCALAPPDATA%\eezmk\epkg
on Windows.
.TP
.B \-g
Global scope: the
.B pkg
and
.B repo
directories next to the
.B ezmk
binary.
.PP
.B pkg install
and
.B repo add
write to one concrete location and therefore accept exactly one scope
flag, defaulting to
.BR \-p .
Query commands accept combinations such as
.B \-pug
and default to all three scopes.
.SH SHORTHANDS
Shorthands are expanded only in the command position
.RB ( "ezmk pb" ,
not
.BR "ezmk project pb" ).
.PP
.nf
.ft CR
pn  project new        ki  pkg install       ra  repo add         wl  workspace list
pb  project build      kr  pkg remove        rr  repo remove      wb  workspace build
pr  project run        ks  pkg search        rl  repo list        wt  workspace test
pc  project clean      kn  pkg info          ru  repo update      wc  workspace clean
pi  project install    kl  pkg list          ri  repo info        ww  workspace watch
pp  project pack       ku  pkg update                            ws  workspace scan
pw  project watch
pt  project test
u   utils              h   help              v   version
.ft R
.fi
.PP
The
.B example
command group deliberately has no shorthand.
.SH OPTION SYNTAX
Options follow GNU conventions:
.TP
.B Long options
.B \-\-flag=value
and
.B \-\-flag value
are equivalent.
.TP
.B Short grouping
.B \-pug
equals
.BR "\-p \-u \-g" .
.TP
.B Attached values
.B \-j4
equals
.BR "\-j 4" .
.TP
.B Interleaving
Options and positional arguments may be mixed freely.
.TP
.B Terminator
Everything after
.B \-\-
is passed through as arguments, for example in
.BR "ezmk run" ,
.BR "ezmk watch \-\-run" ,
.B "ezmk utils"
and the workspace commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EZMK_LANG
Interface language:
.BR en ,
.B zh
or a variant tag such as
.BR zh\-TW .
BCP 47\-style tags are normalized
.RB ( zh_CN ,
.BR zh\-CN ,
.B zh_CN.UTF\-8 ).
Unknown variants fall back to the base language and then to English.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output. Honored only when
.B \-\-color
is left at
.BR auto .
.TP
.B CXX ", " CC
Override the detected C++ and C compiler.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Timestamp used by deterministic builds. Resolution order:
.BR "[compile].source_date_epoch" ,
then this variable, then the git HEAD commit time, then the modification
time of
.BR ezmk.toml .
.TP
.B EDITOR ", " VISUAL
Editor opened to review a legacy shell install hook. Lua install hooks are
sandboxed and never opened, and
.B \-y
skips the editor.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error: missing or invalid configuration, build failure, package or
repository failure, permission denial. A file watcher that stops
unexpectedly also exits with
.BR 1 ;
stopping
.B ezmk watch
with an interrupt exits
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B other
.B ezmk test
exits with the test runner's status, so a failing test suite is reported as
a non\-zero exit code.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ezmk.toml
Project configuration; the only file a project needs.
.TP
.B ezmk.lock
Pinned dependency versions and content hashes, written by
.BR "ezmk pkg install" .
.TP
.B ezmk\-workspace.toml
Workspace member list, options and name.
.TP
.B .ezmk/cache/
Incremental build cache:
.B record.json
plus cached object files.
.TP
.B .ezmk/pkg/
Project\-scope installed packages.
.TP
.B .ezmk/repo/
Project\-scope repository registry and clones.
.TP
.B .ezmk/test\-results/
Default location of test reports requested with
.BR \-\-report .
.TP
.B .ezmk/temp/
Temporary build directory, removed by
.BR "ezmk clean" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ezmk.toml (5)
